meta {
  name: Get Education Board (Student)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/education-boards/{{educationBoardId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  ~course: Science
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{studentAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Fetches one education board's subjects/mark details (name, maxMark,
  passMark, sortOrder per subject) — for showing the subject-wise mark
  entry fields once a student has picked a board via List Education Board
  Names. Requires student authentication.

  Behavior depends on the board's grade:
  - 10th grade: `course` query param is ignored. Response is
    `{ id, name, grade, slug, subjects: [...] }` — the full flat subject
    list (10th-grade boards have no course/stream concept).
  - 12th grade, no `course` given: response is
    `{ id, name, grade, slug, courses: ["Science", "Commerce", ...] }` —
    just the distinct list of streams/courses under this board. Use this
    to populate a course picker before asking for subjects.
  - 12th grade, `course` given: response is
    `{ id, name, grade, slug, isActive, createdAt, updatedAt,
       subjects: [...] }` where `subjects` is filtered to only that
    course's subjects.

  404 if the board doesn't exist OR is currently inactive — a student can
  never view/select a deactivated board's details.
}
